    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i manage a rental property in phoenix and one of the tenants is complaining that their central AC is running all the time but one of the bedrooms stays really warm. the rest of the house seems fine. what are some common reasons why just one room wouldn't be getting enough cool air?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Several factors could cause only one room to stay warm despite the AC running. Poorly sealed windows or doors in that specific bedroom allow warm air to infiltrate, which is a common culprit. Additionally, insufficient airflow due to a blocked vent cover, or issues with the register damper being closed in that room, are frequent causes of uneven cooling. Checking for these simple issues can often resolve the problem quickly.",
      "source": "target",
