    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the vents and they aren't blocked or anything. could it be something hidden inside the ductwork itself that we can't see from the surface? like maybe something buildup or a physical obstruction deeper in the system?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, hidden issues within the ductwork are definitely a possibility. Sediment buildup, bends, or kinks in the ductwork leading specifically to that bedroom can severely restrict airflow. Sometimes, a damper further upstream might be partially stuck in a closed position, redirecting most of the cool air elsewhere. Inspecting the return and supply runs near that bedroom could help pinpoint if the ductwork itself is the problem.",
      "source": "target",
