      "content": "One less obvious cause could be shading or heat load within that specific room, such as poor window insulation letting in excessive solar gain. Another possibility is internal heat sources like electronics or occupants generating more heat than the AC can overcome in that localized area. Furthermore, if the room is on the top floor, attic insulation issues allowing heat transfer from above could be contributing significantly.",
